From 3ceb996bc7b9b2edd7881b29ecb4776d0e6c55ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: turbopack-wasi build <build@turbopack-wasi.invalid>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 22:02:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] turbopack-wasi: run SWC wasm plugins on the embedder's
 WebAssembly engine

experimental.swcPlugins modules are wasm32-wasip1; the wasmtime plugin backend
can't run inside the wasm guest (cap-std/wasi-common don't build there), so both
turbopack-ecmascript-plugins and next-napi-bindings previously swapped in a
NoopRuntime that hard-errored. Replace that stub with swc-plugin-host-bridge: a
Runtime/Instance/Caller implementation that hands the plugin off to a JS driver
worker owning a real WebAssembly engine, rendezvousing through a control block in
the guest's shared linear memory (docs/swc-plugin-host-bridge.md in the outer
repo). Collapse the two duplicate wasm_noop_runtime.rs copies and add the
init_swc_plugin_bridge napi export that registers the host callback.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
